              "type": "numeric",
              "difficulty": "Easy",
              "question": "In triangle ABC, side a = 10, angle A = 30°, and angle B = 45°. Find side b (round to 2 decimal places).",
              "correctNumericAnswer": 14.14,
              "explanation": "By the Law of Sines: b / sin(45°) = 10 / sin(30°). Thus b = 10 * sin(45°) / sin(30°) = 10 * 0.7071 / 0.5 = 14.14.",
              "hints": [
                "Use the formula: a / sin(A) = b / sin(B).",
                "sin(30°) = 0.5 and sin(45°) ≈ 0.7071."
